  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore HttpModel - High-Performance Memory Management Update:\n      - Added 'AllocHeaderOption' (Default: false): Explicitly control when to allocate memory for Map indexing.\n      - Zero-Allocation by Default: Header and Cookie indexing now consume zero heap memory for Map/ByteString until explicitly needed.\n      - Intelligent Lazy Indexing: Implemented incremental indexing for TryGetHeader<T> and TryGetCookie<T>, populating the cache only on-demand (Pay-as-you-go).\n      - Enhanced Memory Safety: Indexing now uses internal buffer Spans to prevent \"Stale Pointer/Memory Drift\" issues during cache buffer resizing.\n      - Improved Data Consistency: Fixed a critical bug where headers were not indexed in builder scenarios without a body.\n      - Performance Boost: Refactored internal lookup logic to minimize comparison overhead for both byte and char spans.",
